\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces \xpg@aux {}{english}A monotonic but not linear point set has a Spearman coefficient $r=1$ even though it has no good linear fit (left). Highly-correlated sequences are recognized by both coefficients (center), but the Pearson coefficient is much more sensitive to outliers (right).\\}}{59}{figure.0.14}\protected@file@percent }
